WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:43.398
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:43.668 --> 00:45.975
[One Meal with Ha Ru: A Chef's Kitchen]

3
00:47.862 --> 00:50.912
And that's today's meal, complete.

4
00:50.912 --> 00:53.569
Today's guest, Yoon Ha Na...

5
01:21.522 --> 01:22.708
[One Meal with Ha Ru: A Chef's Kitchen]

6
01:25.531 --> 01:28.682
I'm in Ha Ru's body again?

7
01:28.682 --> 01:30.737
What is going on this time?

8
01:30.737 --> 01:32.608
[Episode 8]

9
01:32.608 --> 01:34.439
Good, very good!

10
01:34.439 --> 01:35.836
Come on, give it more! Good.

11
01:35.836 --> 01:37.994
One, two... there.

12
01:37.994 --> 01:39.571
Smile! Keep that smile shining. Good.

13
01:39.571 --> 01:41.228
Good, one, two...

14
01:41.228 --> 01:42.928
One more time.

15
01:47.142 --> 01:49.258
Good, now look over here.

16
01:49.258 --> 01:51.208
Twist your arm and bring the product closer to your face.

17
01:51.208 --> 01:53.166
Yeah, that's perfect. Right, one, two.

18
01:53.166 --> 01:55.524
Smile a little for us, good.

19
01:57.236 --> 01:58.822
Look at the camera. Okay, good.

20
01:58.822 --> 02:00.474
One more.

21
02:02.368 --> 02:04.768
Perfect. That's a good shot.

22
02:06.882 --> 02:09.247
One more. Good. One, two...

23
02:11.422 --> 02:13.749
Last one. One, two...

24
02:13.749 --> 02:15.475
Camera. Smile.

25
02:15.475 --> 02:17.067
Finishing shot.

26
02:17.676 --> 02:20.059
You can't talk about actor Jung Woo Jae

27
02:20.059 --> 02:22.699
without mentioning his debut short film, "That Summer, Us."

28
02:22.699 --> 02:26.255
The monster new star who suddenly appeared in Chungmuro, Jung Woo Jae.

29
02:26.255 --> 02:29.702
The fiery eyes that seemed to pop out of the screen

30
02:29.702 --> 02:31.482
still remain the center of attention.

31
02:31.482 --> 02:35.709
Yes, "That Summer, Us," is a film that has truly changed my life.

32
02:35.709 --> 02:39.379
It's all thanks to it that I'm still so loved by you all.

33
02:39.379 --> 02:43.641
Yes, your appearance with actress Yoon Ha Na sure brought a lot of attention.

34
02:43.641 --> 02:45.876
But ever since your debut...

35
02:45.876 --> 02:50.702
- you two haven't worked together again. - Ah, well.

36
02:50.702 --> 02:52.789
It's a shame, but that's just how it is.

37
02:52.789 --> 02:56.146
Could we hope for something to happen in the future?

38
03:01.298 --> 03:04.142
- I can't say for sure. - Well, the fans are hoping...

39
03:04.142 --> 03:09.368
that you have retained that chemistry we saw from "That Summer, Us" in real life.

40
03:09.368 --> 03:11.139
A sort of fantasy, if you will.

41
03:11.139 --> 03:13.608
How are you two faring in real life?

42
03:17.642 --> 03:22.290
Yoon Ha Na has been a very good childhood friend of mine.

43
03:22.888 --> 03:24.695
Now, she is a good colleague,

44
03:24.695 --> 03:27.095
and a good actress.

45
03:27.095 --> 03:28.408
Yeah.

46
03:29.615 --> 03:31.008
[One Meal with Ha Ru: One and Only Table]

47
03:36.082 --> 03:37.742
[Concept] [We focus more on people's stories than food]

48
03:43.075 --> 03:45.155
You came all the way to the set to show me this?

49
03:45.155 --> 03:48.226
Well, not just this.

50
03:48.226 --> 03:49.282
I'm the CEO.

51
03:49.282 --> 03:52.988
I just wanted to know if you had any troubles worth mentioning on the set.

52
03:52.988 --> 03:55.440
I'm here for you, you know!

53
03:56.451 --> 03:59.008
Come, now, hear me out.

54
03:59.008 --> 04:00.469
Wow, would you look at that!

55
04:00.469 --> 04:03.333
Isn't that such an awesome concept?

56
04:03.333 --> 04:09.283
See, "One Meal with Ha Ru" got so popular that the channel wants to go full throttle!

57
04:09.283 --> 04:13.159
The two siblings, Yoon Ha Ru and Yoon Ha Na, go to a special location in their hometown,

58
04:13.159 --> 04:16.989
and invite just one special viewer to share a special meal.

59
04:16.989 --> 04:19.172
Like a secret restaurant, see?

60
04:19.172 --> 04:20.690
Doesn't that sound awesome?

61
04:20.690 --> 04:22.766
Why are you showing me this?

62
04:24.555 --> 04:28.881
- If you could be their first guest... - No.

63
04:29.908 --> 04:33.399
It's nothing hard! Just cook and serve with them.

64
04:33.399 --> 04:35.175
Easy breezy. Rest your mind.

65
04:35.175 --> 04:37.854
Just have a natural conversation and an overall fun time!

66
04:39.028 --> 04:40.559
Easy?

67
04:41.968 --> 04:44.607
Get someone else to do it for you. I can't do it.

68
04:44.607 --> 04:46.535
Jung Woo Jae!

69
04:46.535 --> 04:49.079
Ha Ru is at the peak of his popularity!

70
04:49.079 --> 04:50.779
And Ha Na, as well...

71
04:52.228 --> 04:56.839
Well, appearing in a reality show would really do some good for her.

72
04:56.839 --> 04:58.748
Hey, Jung Woo Jae, you...

73
04:59.351 --> 05:01.688
Come on, just be the wind in their sail, please!

74
05:01.688 --> 05:04.376
Ye Rang. I'm not doing it.

75
05:04.376 --> 05:05.999
I'm telling you.

76
05:11.362 --> 05:13.062
You're still...

77
05:14.282 --> 05:16.194
not over it, are you?

78
05:17.988 --> 05:19.980
What, me?

79
05:19.980 --> 05:22.703
Not you. Ha Ru.

80
05:22.703 --> 05:25.529
Ha Na, you were just today's guest.

81
05:26.922 --> 05:28.960
You're so popular right now,

82
05:28.960 --> 05:33.196
advertisers are dying to get product placement on "One Meal with Ha Ru."

83
05:33.196 --> 05:35.114
That's why we're launching the spin-off,

84
05:35.114 --> 05:39.235
"One and Only Table," right away.

85
05:39.235 --> 05:40.795
"One and Only Table?"

86
05:40.795 --> 05:42.965
- What's that? - Sorry?

87
05:44.074 --> 05:45.682
Hey.

88
05:45.682 --> 05:47.552
Why are you looking at me like that?

89
05:47.552 --> 05:51.586
You're not having second thoughts, are you?

90
05:52.926 --> 05:54.626
No way.

91
06:17.169 --> 06:20.902
[Lost Time]

92
06:28.482 --> 06:31.750
Wow. Guess he's a top star now.

93
06:31.750 --> 06:35.923
Yeah. He must've worked really hard.

94
06:36.516 --> 06:38.632
Look, just amazing.

95
06:38.632 --> 06:40.557
Are you that satisfied with it?

96
06:41.240 --> 06:42.817
You're here.

97
06:42.817 --> 06:44.781
Boss!

98
06:45.426 --> 06:48.300
What's with you? We talked on the phone yesterday.

99
06:56.926 --> 06:58.908
- Woo Jae! - Woo Jae!

100
07:00.746 --> 07:05.860
Oh, I thought you'd go straight there after you finished.

101
07:07.973 --> 07:10.640
I had to drop off some of the crew first.

102
07:10.640 --> 07:12.110
Woo Jae!

103
07:12.733 --> 07:15.377
Wow, Jung Woo Jae!

104
07:15.377 --> 07:16.909
Look at you!

105
07:16.909 --> 07:20.247
Wow, you look amazing!

106
07:21.800 --> 07:23.104
What?

107
07:23.104 --> 07:24.897
Why?

108
07:34.480 --> 07:36.718
We're not that close, are we?

109
07:37.960 --> 07:40.914
Don't touch me.

110
07:46.654 --> 07:48.886
I'll get going.

111
07:48.886 --> 07:50.586
Yeah, sure.

112
08:12.920 --> 08:16.137
Shall we go now?

113
08:17.446 --> 08:18.852
Yeah.

114
08:32.793 --> 08:34.493
Woo Jae said no.

115
08:35.153 --> 08:37.420
How could he just show up right then?

116
08:37.420 --> 08:39.297
What great timing.

117
08:39.960 --> 08:43.144
And why would you grab his waist at that time?

118
08:43.906 --> 08:45.044
Anyway!

119
08:45.044 --> 08:47.712
Let's rethink who the first guest should be.

120
08:49.173 --> 08:50.980
Who could we get?

121
08:51.594 --> 08:54.233
Have you got anyone in mind?

122
08:54.233 --> 08:56.377
What is she talking about right now?

123
08:56.377 --> 08:57.901
Say something!

124
08:57.901 --> 09:00.504
I'm thinking, just keep quiet, will you?

125
09:00.504 --> 09:02.193
Why are you giving me that look? What do you want?

126
09:02.193 --> 09:05.140
Keep your mouth shut and your eyes down if you want to live.

127
09:05.140 --> 09:06.840
What are you guys doing?

128
09:07.540 --> 09:09.064
What's this?

129
09:09.064 --> 09:11.426
Is it some kind of meme?

130
09:11.426 --> 09:12.777
Oh, wait...

131
09:12.777 --> 09:16.034
- Did you just curse at me or something? - No, it's just...

132
09:17.720 --> 09:18.840
[One Meal with Ha Ru: One and Only Table]

133
09:20.693 --> 09:22.808
You're so popular right now,

134
09:22.808 --> 09:25.781
advertisers are dying to get product placement on "One Meal with Ha Ru."

135
09:25.781 --> 09:31.446
That's why we're launching the spin-off, "One and Only Table," right away.

136
09:35.160 --> 09:36.860
So this is it.

137
09:39.605 --> 09:41.476
What should I do?

138
09:45.573 --> 09:49.496
Jung Woo Jae says he'd rather die, and we don't have much time left until we film.

139
09:51.220 --> 09:56.400
First things first, we'll have to film without a guest for the pilot.

140
09:56.400 --> 09:58.050
But...

141
09:58.050 --> 10:01.056
Why won't Woo Jae do it?

142
10:10.033 --> 10:11.932
The reality show...

143
10:11.932 --> 10:13.786
It looked like it'd be fun.

144
10:13.786 --> 10:15.350
If you took the offer,

145
10:15.350 --> 10:17.014
I'd get to visit Haesol in such a long time.

146
10:17.014 --> 10:19.253
Seems nice.

147
10:19.253 --> 10:22.330
We could get Ha Ru's father to cook us up something nice.

148
10:23.113 --> 10:24.677
His mother's raw fish in cold broth is a killer, too.

149
10:24.677 --> 10:28.553
You'd take one sip of that iced broth...

150
10:28.553 --> 10:30.237
so cold it gives you a brain freeze,

151
10:30.237 --> 10:33.046
and the hotness of the sauce comes hitting you right back...

152
10:33.046 --> 10:36.113
Hot and sour, you remember, right? Yoon's raw fish in cold broth!

153
10:36.113 --> 10:38.846
- Keep your eyes on the road. - Oh, sorry.

154
10:41.440 --> 10:43.140
You're still...

155
10:44.880 --> 10:46.913
not over it, are you?

156
10:49.054 --> 10:50.158
Woo Jae.

157
10:50.158 --> 10:53.222
The breakup was ten years ago, not one.

158
10:53.222 --> 10:55.492
You're not 24 anymore, you're 34.

159
10:55.492 --> 10:58.421
I won't force you to do anything you don't want.

160
10:59.080 --> 11:01.246
But after ten whole years...

161
11:01.246 --> 11:04.567
Shouldn't it have gotten better than what it's like right now?

162
11:04.567 --> 11:06.267
Your heart, I mean.

163
11:08.400 --> 11:10.433
Whether you're still in love,

164
11:11.240 --> 11:13.992
or just stubborn and scabbed over...

165
11:15.807 --> 11:18.156
you should come to terms with it now.

166
11:18.741 --> 11:21.030
Do it for the sake of your own heart, Jung Woo Jae.

167
11:43.037 --> 11:44.750
Where are we going, anyway?

168
11:44.750 --> 11:47.834
My schedule is over. Aren't we going home?

169
11:47.834 --> 11:50.459
You have dinner with Gyeong Woo.

170
11:51.837 --> 11:53.297
- I'm good. - "I'm good."

171
11:53.297 --> 11:54.470
"You two go on ahead."

172
11:54.470 --> 11:57.221
That won't fly anymore, you've already said that the last three times.

173
11:57.221 --> 11:59.698
Besides, Pyo Gyeong Woo wants this dinner so bad

174
11:59.698 --> 12:03.082
that he's spent the last hour drinking coffee near the restaurant.

175
12:09.430 --> 12:11.104
But...

176
12:11.104 --> 12:14.052
Why won't Woo Jae do it?

177
12:15.924 --> 12:18.575
What do you mean, why?

178
12:22.084 --> 12:25.084
Oh, no, it's nothing! Nothing to worry about.

179
12:25.084 --> 12:27.064
What is it?

180
12:27.064 --> 12:28.827
What's his reason?

181
12:30.197 --> 12:32.150
- Yoon Ha Ru. - Yeah?

182
12:32.150 --> 12:33.768
Huh?

183
12:33.768 --> 12:37.197
No, not you, Ha Na. Ha Ru. Yoon Ha Ru.

184
12:37.197 --> 12:38.534
Oh, right.

185
12:38.534 --> 12:40.205
Yeah.

186
12:40.205 --> 12:41.635
What is it?

187
12:42.284 --> 12:43.908
Why is she staring like that?

188
12:43.908 --> 12:46.379
Did she... catch on to something?

189
12:47.970 --> 12:49.670
Babe.

190
12:50.384 --> 12:53.670
Could you just shut up for ten seconds, please?

191
12:53.670 --> 12:56.467
Oh, who's a good boy?

192
12:58.404 --> 13:02.482
I'm not even married yet, but it seems like I've already got a son.

193
13:05.574 --> 13:08.151
Well, Ha Na.

194
13:10.407 --> 13:12.131
You and Woo Jae...

195
13:12.131 --> 13:15.103
It may have been ten years since you guys broke up,

196
13:15.103 --> 13:17.366
but I still think you need to be more thoughtful.

197
13:17.366 --> 13:20.520
And speaking of thoughtfulness between ex-lovers,

198
13:20.520 --> 13:24.284
I think it'd be fairer for the one who got over faster to be the more mindful one.

199
13:24.284 --> 13:26.008
For example, what you just did back there,

200
13:26.008 --> 13:29.372
- touching him, would make him feel... - Does she mean Woo Jae and I broke up?

201
13:29.372 --> 13:31.833
And I'm the one who caused it?

202
13:34.820 --> 13:36.544
Just a moment.

203
13:36.544 --> 13:37.990
Hello?

204
13:42.830 --> 13:45.524
- I told you that schedule is not going to work! - You need to go, now.

205
13:45.524 --> 13:47.320
- Me? - Woo Jae's new movie

206
13:47.320 --> 13:49.308
- starts shooting next month, and... - I don't know.

207
13:49.308 --> 13:52.814
the overseas promotion for the last series, on top of that,

208
13:52.814 --> 13:55.815
we need three days just for moving!

209
13:56.907 --> 13:58.491
- What do I do? - We need to go together.

210
13:58.491 --> 14:01.255
- Take me with you. - Do you really think that?

211
14:01.255 --> 14:05.140
If you offer a higher fee, we'll operate everything?

212
14:05.140 --> 14:07.424
No, that's not how it works.

213
14:07.424 --> 14:08.856
- Hey, you know what? - Excuse me.

214
14:08.856 --> 14:12.860
- Instead of trying to convince me on the phone, - Wait, wait!

215
14:12.860 --> 14:14.051
What do I do?

216
14:14.051 --> 14:17.552
why don't you go back and work out the schedule again?

217
14:39.207 --> 14:42.767
[Lost Time]

218
14:43.714 --> 14:45.438
Let's start now.

219
14:45.438 --> 14:47.738
Ready... Action!

220
14:48.794 --> 14:52.114
So you want me to take stuff out of the bag

221
14:52.114 --> 14:55.114
and show it to you, is that right?

222
14:55.114 --> 14:57.240
Okay. Kind of pointless, but sure.

223
14:58.420 --> 15:00.867
Hello. Say hello!

224
15:00.867 --> 15:01.923
Oh, okay.

225
15:01.923 --> 15:02.933
[Hi to the camera]

226
15:02.933 --> 15:05.264
Yeah, hi, hi.

227
15:05.264 --> 15:07.148
Hello, or whatever.

228
15:09.000 --> 15:11.749
I'll do... whatever this is, today!

229
15:21.767 --> 15:23.427
It's a hat.

230
15:23.427 --> 15:26.324
Probably for days when I haven't washed my hair.

231
15:26.324 --> 15:29.000
To protect others' eyes and noses...

232
15:29.000 --> 15:32.449
from my odor, you see.

233
15:33.094 --> 15:34.534
In fact, Yoon Ha Na...

234
15:34.534 --> 15:36.518
No, no. I mean, I...

235
15:36.518 --> 15:41.144
I don't wash my hair very much on my days off.

236
15:43.874 --> 15:45.000
Let's see...

237
15:46.300 --> 15:47.998
Sunglasses. I see.

238
15:47.998 --> 15:51.788
Ah! I know. These are for hiding my face without makeup.

239
15:51.788 --> 15:54.110
Or... Maybe not.

240
15:54.110 --> 15:56.497
Maybe it's for glaring at people.

241
15:58.314 --> 16:01.398
Guys, can you see my eyes right now?

242
16:01.398 --> 16:03.255
You can't, right?

243
16:03.255 --> 16:06.199
There's always something that pisses you off at work.

244
16:06.199 --> 16:08.450
That's where these come in.

245
16:08.450 --> 16:10.036
To glare at people.

246
16:11.400 --> 16:14.534
Now, let's see what we've got here.

247
16:14.534 --> 16:17.144
Here we have a keychain.

248
16:17.144 --> 16:18.844
It's...

249
16:24.294 --> 16:25.934
Now...

250
16:25.934 --> 16:31.158
You can, of course, just eat this tender charcoal-grilled beef as is,

251
16:31.158 --> 16:34.708
but if you drink this 80-year-old-recipe Pyongyang cold noodle broth with it,

252
16:34.708 --> 16:37.069
it's good enough to kill! See?

253
16:40.814 --> 16:44.389
[One Meal with Ha Ru: One and Only Table] Big announcement incoming!

254
16:44.389 --> 16:46.814
- The popular cooking show - The trailer is out already.

255
16:46.814 --> 16:48.349
that took the nation by hunger,

256
16:48.349 --> 16:50.042
"One and Only Table!"

257
16:50.042 --> 16:51.499
- Coming soon! - What's the deal with Ha Na?

258
16:51.499 --> 16:54.397
She just doesn't seem to grow old.

259
16:55.903 --> 16:58.487
What do you think her secret is?

260
16:58.487 --> 17:00.544
- Hey, have some of this meat, too. - It's amazing how good she looks.

261
17:00.544 --> 17:02.002
You've just been drinking this whole time.

262
17:02.002 --> 17:04.225
- But I am eating. - She hasn't changed a bit.

263
17:06.554 --> 17:08.684
Come to think of it, what's it been?

264
17:08.684 --> 17:10.255
Ten years?

265
17:10.255 --> 17:11.467
It's been ten years, right?

266
17:11.467 --> 17:13.027
Okay.

267
17:13.027 --> 17:14.678
I can say it with ease now.

268
17:14.678 --> 17:16.720
If I'm being honest, you...

269
17:17.494 --> 17:19.798
When I heard you and Ha Na were dating, well, I...

270
17:19.798 --> 17:21.262
I was so jealous!

271
17:21.262 --> 17:23.159
Tell me, dating a goddess like that...

272
17:23.159 --> 17:25.174
What does it feel like?

273
17:25.174 --> 17:27.318
Does the world bloom with beauty?

274
17:27.318 --> 17:29.959
I doubt you ever got mad when you were together.

275
17:33.314 --> 17:36.158
Anyway, why did you two even break up?

276
17:36.158 --> 17:38.642
You were perfect together! Good-looking guy meets good-looking girl,

277
17:38.642 --> 17:41.656
- gets married... - Hey, have this 80-year-old-recipe dumpling!

278
17:43.959 --> 17:46.467
Have some more beef.

279
17:50.140 --> 17:53.441
It was like they were in a movie since their first day together.

280
17:54.047 --> 17:58.567
There are only a few moments in my life that I just can't forget,

281
17:58.567 --> 18:00.267
and that day is one of them.

282
18:00.887 --> 18:03.294
Why? What was it like?

283
18:03.294 --> 18:04.938
Don't you remember, babe?

284
18:04.938 --> 18:07.024
We saw it together.

285
18:10.140 --> 18:12.632
I must be getting old.

286
18:13.527 --> 18:16.000
I forgot what happened.

287
18:16.000 --> 18:19.859
It was back in our university years, when they were filming that short film.

288
18:20.567 --> 18:23.826
- Yeah? - They had a really intense fight!

289
18:27.500 --> 18:28.951
But what about me?

290
18:28.951 --> 18:30.714
How do you think that makes me feel?

291
18:30.714 --> 18:33.351
Like I'm helpless. Like all I do is cause trouble.

292
18:33.351 --> 18:35.094
That's...

293
18:35.094 --> 18:37.200
That's what you make me feel like.

294
18:37.807 --> 18:39.500
I'm asking you.

295
18:39.500 --> 18:40.958
Please.

296
18:40.958 --> 18:43.235
Just live for yourself.

297
18:43.235 --> 18:45.826
They were throwing such harsh words at each other,

298
18:45.826 --> 18:48.282
when Lee Hyeong Won showed up.

299
18:50.800 --> 18:55.398
Right as I thought I might get to witness a dopamine-filled love triangle in real life...

300
18:55.398 --> 18:56.986
Yoon Ha Na!

301
19:43.221 --> 19:44.432
Ha Na.

302
19:44.432 --> 19:45.871
Are you okay?

303
19:49.461 --> 19:50.932
With just one hug from Woo Jae,

304
19:50.932 --> 19:53.314
the whole vibe changed.

305
19:54.308 --> 19:55.738
Yeah.

306
19:59.608 --> 20:01.697
I'm sorry, Ha Na.

307
20:02.348 --> 20:05.458
- I didn't mean to get into a fight... - I like you.

308
20:09.881 --> 20:11.327
I...

309
20:12.304 --> 20:14.700
I like you. Jung Woo Jae.

310
20:43.104 --> 20:45.588
While they were dating,

311
20:45.588 --> 20:47.538
what were they like?

312
20:47.538 --> 20:49.238
Did they seem happy?

313
20:52.764 --> 20:54.755
It was like the whole world...

314
20:54.755 --> 20:57.363
was an island with just the two of them living on it.

315
20:57.991 --> 21:00.924
Devoid of any outside noise.

316
21:00.924 --> 21:04.121
A darn pretty island, I'd say.

317
21:12.304 --> 21:15.054
- That sounds good! I'm starving. - You must be hungry.

318
21:15.054 --> 21:17.278
- What do you want to eat? - I want meat!

319
21:17.278 --> 21:18.311
- Meat? - Yeah.

320
21:18.311 --> 21:19.705
Oh, wait.

321
21:36.878 --> 21:38.808
What are you hiding?

322
21:38.808 --> 21:40.474
Ta-da!

323
21:51.051 --> 21:52.573
It tickles!

324
21:53.484 --> 21:55.184
What are you doing?

325
21:58.791 --> 22:01.190
- This is awful! - Hey, babe.

326
22:05.004 --> 22:07.118
Babe! Babe!

327
22:08.658 --> 22:10.129
What was that?

328
22:12.504 --> 22:13.966
What are you looking at?

329
22:23.264 --> 22:29.762
We're here today with Jung Woo Jae, who stole every woman's heart

330
22:29.762 --> 22:32.021
with the 2017 drama, "The Boy from the Moon."

331
22:32.021 --> 22:34.608
This may be a touchy subject,

332
22:34.608 --> 22:39.090
but everyone is just dying to know, so I can't help but ask.

333
22:39.090 --> 22:43.557
Do you, perhaps, have a girlfriend?

334
22:47.014 --> 22:49.490
Yes, I do.

335
22:49.490 --> 22:51.371
We definitely weren't expecting that.

336
22:51.371 --> 22:54.479
Are we the first to officially hear about this?

337
22:54.479 --> 22:58.306
Yeah, I'd say so. We're doing great.

338
22:58.959 --> 23:00.664
[The Masked Season] Next up...

339
23:00.664 --> 23:06.490
We have with us the actress Yoon Ha Na, nicknamed the Jeon Hee Ae of short films.

340
23:06.490 --> 23:08.827
We are taking questions now.

341
23:09.838 --> 23:15.743
This is your first appearance in a title role in a drama with "The Masked Season."

342
23:15.743 --> 23:19.055
However, some have compared you with the other actors, Jeon Hee Ae and Ha Dong Jin,

343
23:19.055 --> 23:22.692
voicing concerns about the difference in your proficiency in acting.

344
23:22.692 --> 23:28.294
We want to know if you felt like you were lacking skills yourself.

345
23:31.962 --> 23:34.080
Well, first of all,

346
23:34.080 --> 23:38.541
I was grateful to be able to work side-by-side with such big names.

347
23:38.541 --> 23:40.700
It was a true honor.

348
23:41.470 --> 23:48.373
I tried my best not to get in the way of my seniors and colleagues.

349
23:48.373 --> 23:51.704
I hope you'll take kindly to my efforts.

350
23:53.783 --> 23:57.248
You just mentioned "a difference in proficiency," yes?

351
23:58.810 --> 24:04.749
Truthfully speaking, both Hee Ae and I were in awe of how good Ha Na's acting was on set.

352
24:04.749 --> 24:07.702
Her ability to read intentions beyond what is shown,

353
24:07.702 --> 24:12.469
and her almost explosive charisma that takes over the whole set.

354
24:12.469 --> 24:14.375
If I may say so,

355
24:14.375 --> 24:20.358
I truly think that I was lucky to have had actress Yoon Ha Na as my counterpart.

356
24:20.358 --> 24:23.231
Actress Yoon Ha Na is, promptly speaking,

357
24:23.231 --> 24:28.212
an actress of great proficiency who helped me step beyond my own shortcomings.

358
24:32.238 --> 24:34.242
The expertise of an actor

359
24:34.242 --> 24:38.240
isn't determined by the length of their career or resume.

360
24:38.240 --> 24:45.099
You'll have to see Yoon Ha Na's acting skills for yourself when the program airs.

361
24:49.947 --> 24:52.097
Any more questions?

362
24:54.502 --> 24:55.840
Ms. Yoon Ha Na!

363
24:55.840 --> 25:00.480
Just now, actor Jung Woo Jae admitted to a love scandal on a live interview.

364
25:00.480 --> 25:04.881
Everyone is pointing you out as the missing piece.

365
25:04.881 --> 25:07.603
Is there any truth to this?

366
25:25.837 --> 25:30.274
This is my first time hearing about this as well.

367
25:30.921 --> 25:33.198
Mr. Jung Woo Jae is...

368
25:37.591 --> 25:42.251
Just a longtime childhood friend of mine.

369
25:42.251 --> 25:45.328
He's a great actor, that's all I think of him.

370
25:45.328 --> 25:47.122
I ask you not to make any more assumptions,

371
25:47.122 --> 25:51.809
and to stay on the topic of our show, "The Masked Season."

372
25:53.489 --> 25:55.868
Any other questions?

373
26:01.602 --> 26:03.710
What do you want to do?

374
26:03.710 --> 26:07.970
I'll clean up after you, but the decision is yours.

375
26:15.017 --> 26:16.961
I'm sorry.

376
26:16.961 --> 26:18.901
I wasn't thinking straight.

377
26:18.901 --> 26:21.323
I should've asked you first.

378
26:21.935 --> 26:24.027
No, I'm sorry.

379
26:24.027 --> 26:25.810
I was just so...

380
26:25.810 --> 26:28.856
caught off guard, and it scared me.

381
26:28.856 --> 26:31.005
I didn't mean to lie.

382
26:32.787 --> 26:35.069
You guys are so dramatic.

383
26:43.229 --> 26:46.347
If we admit it now and change our statement,

384
26:46.347 --> 26:49.118
it would make Ha Na a liar.

385
26:50.855 --> 26:55.686
I want to keep who I'm dating a secret.

386
26:55.686 --> 26:57.810
You'd do that for us, right?

387
26:59.940 --> 27:01.374
Sure.

388
27:02.691 --> 27:05.522
I'm so sorry, Woo Jae.

389
27:05.522 --> 27:07.798
No, I'm the one who should be sorry.

390
27:07.798 --> 27:10.444
You just focus on your show, okay?

391
27:12.096 --> 27:14.293
Why are you crying?

392
27:14.293 --> 27:16.318
- Hey, don't cry. - I'm really sorry.

393
27:16.318 --> 27:18.291
No, I'm sorry.

394
27:19.835 --> 27:21.535
Hey, don't cry.

395
27:22.230 --> 27:24.870
They were inseparable like that, but...

396
27:51.938 --> 27:53.962
Did Yoon Ha Na...

397
27:53.962 --> 27:57.022
do something really bad or something?

398
27:59.918 --> 28:05.091
I've just been having some trouble remembering things these days.

399
28:05.091 --> 28:09.308
Well, she must've had her reasons.

400
28:09.308 --> 28:13.872
But for Woo Jae, it must've felt like she denied his whole existence.

401
28:13.872 --> 28:17.198
He went away to serve in the army at the peak of his popularity,

402
28:17.198 --> 28:20.698
and I couldn't even stop him. He seemed so miserable.

403
28:20.698 --> 28:22.235
Denied?

404
28:22.235 --> 28:24.622
It's whatever. Let's stop talking about those two.

405
28:24.622 --> 28:27.571
- W-wait, I... - Anyway, babe?

406
28:27.571 --> 28:30.375
- Yeah? - We...

407
28:30.375 --> 28:32.985
have some catching up to do, don't you think?

408
28:36.071 --> 28:37.384
What do you mean?

409
28:37.384 --> 28:39.291
What do you think?

410
28:39.291 --> 28:42.002
Let's move on from others' love lives...

411
28:43.624 --> 28:45.979
and into ours now.

412
28:49.568 --> 28:51.586
Babe.

413
28:51.586 --> 28:53.745
You're not going home tonight.

414
29:02.841 --> 29:04.318
Hey!

415
29:04.958 --> 29:06.631
I...

416
29:07.242 --> 29:09.291
It's...

417
29:10.482 --> 29:12.988
- What? - I mean...

418
29:12.988 --> 29:14.655
I just...

419
29:14.655 --> 29:16.106
I'm saying...

420
29:16.106 --> 29:19.901
This can't be happening. How do I get out of this?

421
29:20.842 --> 29:22.461
I love you.

422
29:23.822 --> 29:26.762
I really love you, Seo Ye Rang...

423
29:26.762 --> 29:28.695
But I...

424
29:28.695 --> 29:30.474
I'm like...

425
29:32.508 --> 29:34.319
Really...

426
29:34.319 --> 29:37.110
- I'm not feeling good today. - Huh?

427
29:37.110 --> 29:39.822
You're sick? Why? How?

428
29:39.822 --> 29:42.852
Well, I'm feeling...

429
29:42.852 --> 29:46.029
Tell me! Where does it hurt?

430
29:47.262 --> 29:49.444
Actually, I'm...

431
29:51.175 --> 29:52.646
Never mind.

432
29:52.646 --> 29:55.744
If I tell you, I'll just make you sad.

433
29:58.015 --> 30:01.659
I'll tell you tomorrow.

434
30:01.659 --> 30:03.322
- Tomorrow. - Tomorrow?

435
30:03.322 --> 30:07.288
Yes! I'll just get going now.

436
30:08.208 --> 30:09.955
I'll call you!

437
30:09.955 --> 30:11.846
Y-you're leaving like this?

438
30:12.648 --> 30:15.918
I'm sorry, Yoon Ha Ru. Sorry, Ye Rang!

439
30:18.668 --> 30:20.368
Hey!

440
30:21.388 --> 30:23.615
That bastard!

441
30:23.615 --> 30:25.953
He better not be cheating!

442
30:33.522 --> 30:36.986
If you check the seat pocket, there's a script for you.

443
30:36.986 --> 30:38.686
Oh, this?

444
30:40.404 --> 30:41.780
[Lost Time, Written by Chu Si Hwan] "Lost Time?"

445
30:41.780 --> 30:43.573
It's a new script.

446
30:43.573 --> 30:45.926
The director only wanted you to have it.

447
30:45.926 --> 30:47.504
- Is that so? - Yeah.

448
30:47.504 --> 30:50.061
It's a rookie director, I heard. Take a look.

449
30:50.061 --> 30:54.552
The development team said it's the best one they've had come in the whole year!

450
30:54.552 --> 30:56.929
- Sure, I'll check it out. - Yes, ma'am!

451
30:56.929 --> 30:59.266
And before you shoot the reality show in two days,

452
30:59.266 --> 31:01.893
the CEO arranged a meeting with the director.

453
31:01.893 --> 31:03.344
Okay, okay.

454
31:03.344 --> 31:07.933
Our Boss really likes to keep a tight schedule.

455
31:40.773 --> 31:42.946
Woo Jae, just let it go already.

456
31:42.946 --> 31:46.750
I'll get you something nicer, please?

457
31:46.750 --> 31:49.167
Good job today. You can go home now.

458
31:49.167 --> 31:51.451
Seriously, this isn't an antique shop!

459
31:51.451 --> 31:53.852
There's plenty of ready-made stuff that gets the job done!

460
31:53.852 --> 31:55.687
Go away.

461
31:55.687 --> 31:56.791
Okay.

462
31:58.620 --> 32:00.173
What's wrong?

463
32:00.173 --> 32:02.986
Give it over here, I'll do it for you.

464
32:02.986 --> 32:05.110
- What are you doing? - No way.

465
32:05.110 --> 32:08.820
It only has meaning if I made every last bit myself.

466
32:08.820 --> 32:11.517
Do whatever you want. I'm going.

467
32:11.517 --> 32:13.109
Just go easy on it and go to bed on time.

468
32:13.109 --> 32:15.555
Thanks for putting up with me.

469
32:47.353 --> 32:49.053
They're perfect.

470
33:02.379 --> 33:03.813
- This way. - Huh?

471
33:03.813 --> 33:05.812
- What is it? - Come on.

472
33:21.186 --> 33:22.630
What's this?

473
33:22.630 --> 33:23.977
Open it.

474
33:24.632 --> 33:26.332
What could it be?

475
33:37.286 --> 33:38.700
What do you think?

476
33:40.740 --> 33:43.528
Did you make this yourself?

477
33:43.528 --> 33:45.000
Yes. I...

478
33:45.000 --> 33:47.924
I wanted to make the pinnacle of the analog and vintage aesthetic.

479
33:47.924 --> 33:50.175
There's just one in this world.

480
33:51.686 --> 33:55.163
Analog and vintage aesthetic.

481
34:01.260 --> 34:02.697
Hi.

482
34:07.736 --> 34:09.436
Hey, Jung Woo Jae.

483
34:12.490 --> 34:14.463
This is unbelievable.

484
34:16.976 --> 34:18.450
Ha Na?

485
34:18.450 --> 34:19.775
What's the matter?

486
34:20.463 --> 34:22.571
I just can't with you anymore.

487
34:25.463 --> 34:29.824
I guess you don't like the vintage aesthetic...

488
34:36.203 --> 34:37.807
I can't with you...

489
34:37.807 --> 34:40.435
being so cute!

490
34:40.435 --> 34:42.536
I'm... cute?

491
34:42.536 --> 34:45.315
So cute that I can't hold it in anymore.

492
34:46.016 --> 34:50.038
This keychain is so, so cute, too!

493
34:51.970 --> 34:54.907
I'll cherish it forever, until I die!

494
34:54.907 --> 34:56.878
In fact, when the Grim Reaper comes for me,

495
34:56.878 --> 34:59.416
I'll ask him to let me take it with me.

496
34:59.416 --> 35:02.592
The Grim Reaper? Now that's a stretch.

497
35:11.829 --> 35:13.526
Thank you.

498
35:13.526 --> 35:14.986
Thank you, too.

499
35:14.986 --> 35:16.393
I love it so much.

500
35:16.393 --> 35:18.093
- Really? - Yeah.

501
36:43.846 --> 36:46.680
What do I do now?

502
37:14.240 --> 37:15.940
[Yoon Ha Na, 2013 Best New Actress, 2022 Best Supporting Actress]

503
37:16.553 --> 37:18.091
That's all?

504
37:18.091 --> 37:20.210
Where's her Best Actress Award?

505
37:25.893 --> 37:28.626
"Failed to secure a leading role?"

506
37:28.626 --> 37:30.937
"Made her career as a high-end supporting actress?"

507
37:30.937 --> 37:32.452
Woah.

508
37:34.360 --> 37:36.166
[Baekryong Film Awards terrorism]

509
37:38.133 --> 37:40.393
[Actor Hyun Seong Jae, Fashion Terrorist?] [Terror on the Red Carpet, the Actress who Fell]

510
37:43.173 --> 37:45.993
So this is how it changed this time.

511
37:45.993 --> 37:47.706
Wait a minute.

512
37:47.706 --> 37:49.164
Then...

513
37:50.693 --> 37:52.066
[Lee Hyeong Won]

514
37:53.366 --> 37:55.044
[Lee Hyeong Won, 2026 Arcadia Gold Medalist]

515
37:55.044 --> 37:59.577
Darn it, so he took my gold medal!

516
38:03.093 --> 38:04.853
["Judo Hero" Lee Hyeong Won Disappears: Why?] Disappeared?

517
38:07.720 --> 38:08.865
[Account Unavailable]

518
38:10.726 --> 38:12.952
It's got to be this bastard.

519
38:12.952 --> 38:14.652
Lee Hyeong Won...

520
38:17.726 --> 38:19.544
- There you are. - Where's the camcorder?

521
38:19.544 --> 38:20.614
- In your room. - Okay.

522
38:20.614 --> 38:22.314
No, not there!

523
38:23.926 --> 38:25.449
That one.

524
38:51.386 --> 38:55.640
Well... it does seem that the situation has changed a little.

525
39:06.180 --> 39:09.127
What could I have possibly done to Woo Jae?

526
39:14.093 --> 39:15.577
Hey.

527
39:18.440 --> 39:19.857
What?

528
39:19.857 --> 39:21.557
Are you okay?

529
39:23.373 --> 39:25.497
Why wouldn't I be?

530
39:25.497 --> 39:27.368
Woo Jae is well and alive.

531
39:27.368 --> 39:29.099
You seem successful.

532
39:29.099 --> 39:30.652
And me...

533
39:31.713 --> 39:33.164
Well.

534
39:33.164 --> 39:37.234
I'm still acting, at least.

535
39:39.786 --> 39:41.190
What now?

536
39:41.190 --> 39:44.001
What's with that face? It's not like you to look so melancholic.

537
39:44.001 --> 39:47.140
I mean, your career as an actress aside,

538
39:47.140 --> 39:51.237
it kind of feels like I took your house away, you know.

539
39:51.237 --> 39:53.881
"Took it away?" You've got to be kidding me.

540
39:53.881 --> 39:57.584
At least you're letting me live with you.

541
39:59.980 --> 40:01.380
Hey, I'm your big brother.

542
40:01.380 --> 40:04.300
Just say the word, and I'll buy you any house you want.

543
40:08.073 --> 40:10.496
About you quitting judo...

544
40:11.673 --> 40:13.938
I really was sorry.

545
40:18.140 --> 40:19.844
I guess winners win, though.

546
40:19.844 --> 40:23.505
You sure are something, Yoon Ha Ru. You've made it as a chef, too.

547
40:24.100 --> 40:25.800
You've grown well.

548
40:29.593 --> 40:32.959
I sorted some things out while waiting for you.

549
40:34.620 --> 40:38.053
I never thought I'd see the day Yoon Ha Ru grew up.

550
40:39.034 --> 40:40.733
First of all, how we returned to the present...

551
40:40.733 --> 40:42.580
[Remove battery: present, next leap: 2017] is clear now.

552
40:42.580 --> 40:43.946
The removal of the battery.

553
40:43.946 --> 40:45.970
Where do you think you're touching, you bastard?

554
40:45.970 --> 40:48.333
Woah, what the heck!

555
40:51.933 --> 40:53.773
If we travel to the past again,

556
40:53.773 --> 40:55.824
it'll probably be to the year 2017.

557
40:55.824 --> 40:57.914
Yeah. The only video left

558
40:57.914 --> 41:00.183
[2017 is the only thumbnail left] is from 2017.

559
41:02.246 --> 41:04.504
The Best Actress Award...

560
41:04.504 --> 41:07.094
went to some other actress.

561
41:07.094 --> 41:10.378
The movie that you got the award for was gone in the first place.

562
41:13.240 --> 41:14.524
It's fine.

563
41:14.524 --> 41:16.768
As long as Woo Jae is safe.

564
41:16.768 --> 41:18.452
And...

565
41:18.452 --> 41:20.152
This bastard.

566
41:20.794 --> 41:23.044
[Lee Hyeong Won] "Arcadia Gold Medalist?"

567
41:23.044 --> 41:24.848
He retired after winning that gold medal.

568
41:24.848 --> 41:26.548
Dropped off the face of the earth.

569
41:28.120 --> 41:29.580
Disappeared?

570
41:29.580 --> 41:31.824
[We're back in the actual present time now] Yeah, it was all Lee Hyeong Won, that bastard.

571
41:31.824 --> 41:34.178
The stalking, Woo Jae's death... all of it.

572
41:34.178 --> 41:36.535
Something was going on even back then.

573
41:39.340 --> 41:40.684
But something's off.

574
41:40.684 --> 41:43.633
Hyeong Won wasn't there to hurt me that day.

575
41:43.633 --> 41:45.270
What?

576
41:45.270 --> 41:46.814
Explain what you meant by that.

577
41:46.814 --> 41:51.155
If he wasn't there to hurt you, why did he suddenly show up in Haesol?

578
41:53.266 --> 41:54.737
Give it back.

579
41:54.737 --> 41:57.210
No, it's too dangerous.

580
41:57.210 --> 41:58.768
What?

581
41:59.401 --> 42:01.632
If you keep holding onto this, Yoon Ha Na...

582
42:01.632 --> 42:03.332
You'll be in danger.

583
42:07.909 --> 42:09.120
Lee Hyeong Won...

584
42:09.120 --> 42:12.234
Apparently the coach and the chancellor stopped him from taking part in the movie,

585
42:12.234 --> 42:16.201
which he worked so hard for, you know.

586
42:16.201 --> 42:19.796
He lost the male lead role, and it just wasn't fair to him.

587
42:19.796 --> 42:22.281
He was really bummed out about it.

588
42:23.167 --> 42:25.507
He must have been feeling conflicted about the whole thing,

589
42:25.507 --> 42:28.107
so he was just wandering around near the practice room...

590
42:28.107 --> 42:33.072
That's when he saw someone suspicious.

591
42:33.072 --> 42:34.826
Suspicious?

592
42:38.130 --> 42:39.240
Yeah.

593
42:39.240 --> 42:41.558
He saw someone open my locker...

594
42:41.558 --> 42:44.242
and swap out my camcorder for a different one.

595
42:44.983 --> 42:47.423
Lee Hyeong Won happened to witness it.

596
43:11.663 --> 43:12.896
[Yoon Ha Na]

597
43:12.896 --> 43:14.596
Yoon Ha Na's locker?

598
43:15.756 --> 43:17.456
That bastard!

599
43:22.150 --> 43:23.669
Hey, you.

600
43:51.310 --> 43:53.010
[Yoon Ha Na]

601
43:54.646 --> 43:56.876
So he got the camcorder back.

602
43:56.876 --> 43:58.576
Did he see the bastard's face?

603
43:59.616 --> 44:01.622
No, he didn't.

604
44:01.622 --> 44:05.944
So, Lee Hyeong Won had the camcorder, but didn't return it to you right away,

605
44:05.944 --> 44:09.988
and showed up at the filming set to say it was because you'd be in danger?

606
44:09.988 --> 44:11.226
Do you seriously believe that?

607
44:11.226 --> 44:13.943
That Lee Hyeong Won isn't the one after the camcorder?

608
44:13.943 --> 44:15.743
That's rich.

609
44:15.743 --> 44:18.780
Say we give him the benefit of the doubt, and believe he wasn't after the camcorder.

610
44:18.780 --> 44:22.752
What does it even matter, when Lee Hyeong Won killed Woo Jae?

611
44:23.470 --> 44:25.307
I guess.

612
44:25.307 --> 44:27.958
I was just so taken aback at the time.

613
44:27.958 --> 44:31.112
But you're right, he could've been lying.

614
44:31.836 --> 44:33.423
Lee Hyeong Won...

615
44:33.423 --> 44:36.763
We don't know what he could be planning as we speak.

616
44:36.763 --> 44:40.358
The good news is that Woo Jae is well and alive,

617
44:40.358 --> 44:42.989
and you weren't threatened at the award ceremony.

618
44:43.643 --> 44:46.847
Sure, we're in each other's bodies, and that is a problem.

619
44:46.847 --> 44:51.032
Worse than that, the biggest variable posed to us is...

620
44:52.983 --> 44:54.683
- Lee Hyeong Won. - Lee Hyeong Won.

621
45:09.096 --> 45:10.796
Damn it!

622
45:28.290 --> 45:31.149
- Good job, everyone. - Good work, everyone.

623
45:32.315 --> 45:35.265
- Good work today. - Good job.

624
45:35.265 --> 45:37.211
What are you doing on your day off tomorrow?

625
45:37.211 --> 45:39.283
Just resting. You should take a rest, too.

626
45:39.283 --> 45:40.990
This is your first break in a month.

627
45:40.990 --> 45:42.954
I heard Ha Ru is going to Haesol.

628
45:42.954 --> 45:46.282
He's going to do some research and a pre-interview.

629
45:46.282 --> 45:48.390
I was thinking of going with him.

630
45:49.050 --> 45:53.156
I'm guessing you wouldn't want to go.

631
45:54.123 --> 45:55.350
Yeah.

632
45:55.350 --> 45:57.663
I changed my mind. I don't want to go!

633
45:57.663 --> 46:00.780
I didn't really want to go anyway.

634
46:00.780 --> 46:03.943
Right, you have a new script.

635
46:03.943 --> 46:05.200
Okay.

636
46:05.200 --> 46:06.416
Who's the director?

637
46:06.416 --> 46:09.567
It's a rookie, one I've never heard of before.

638
46:09.567 --> 46:11.458
The development team is losing it over this one.

639
46:11.458 --> 46:14.797
They said it's even better than Director Na Bong Chang's newest work.

640
46:15.505 --> 46:17.310
I'll give it a read.

641
46:17.310 --> 46:21.115
But from what I heard, a copy went to Ha Na as well.

642
46:22.776 --> 46:24.280
The director...

643
46:24.280 --> 46:28.443
really wants you and Ha Na to film it together.

644
46:28.443 --> 46:29.874
That's what he wants.

645
46:35.230 --> 46:36.557
Is that so?

646
46:37.990 --> 46:39.690
Let's go, Woo Jae!

647
46:57.503 --> 47:00.663
[Lost Time]

648
47:10.870 --> 47:13.407
Wow, Seok Min, you're good at your job!

649
47:13.407 --> 47:15.757
- This coffee is amazing! - Huh?

650
47:16.423 --> 47:19.830
It's just your favorite brand, the one you always have.

651
47:19.830 --> 47:21.530
My favorite brand?

652
47:23.796 --> 47:26.489
Yoon Ha Na's taste buds aren't that bad after all, huh?

653
47:27.190 --> 47:28.890
Whatever.

654
47:30.516 --> 47:33.739
Right, Ha Na. How did you like "Lost Time?"

655
47:34.376 --> 47:35.950
"Lost Time?"

656
47:35.950 --> 47:38.547
Yeah, the movie script I gave you last time.

657
47:38.547 --> 47:41.123
There's a meeting with the director today, before the shoot.

658
47:41.123 --> 47:43.201
I told you last time.

659
47:45.663 --> 47:48.583
Oh, that!

660
47:48.583 --> 47:50.588
You didn't read it yet?

661
47:50.588 --> 47:53.968
Sorry, I'll read it now.

662
48:01.676 --> 48:04.350
[Lost Time, Written by Chu Si Hwan]

663
48:26.010 --> 48:27.438
Hey.

664
48:29.270 --> 48:31.257
What's that? It smells great.

665
48:31.257 --> 48:32.982
These.

666
48:33.570 --> 48:35.147
I like them.

667
48:35.147 --> 48:36.847
You need your coffee, right?

668
48:54.683 --> 48:58.107
Your coffee, sir.

669
48:58.107 --> 49:00.504
Here, the script for "Lost Time," the one I told you about.

670
49:00.504 --> 49:04.011
[Lost Time, Written by Chu Si Hwan]

671
49:23.096 --> 49:24.342
[Eun Soo, still mourning Yeong Hyeon,]

672
49:24.342 --> 49:26.802
[finds an old camcorder in the closet.] "An old camcorder..."

673
49:43.456 --> 49:45.527
He must be out of his mind.

674
49:45.527 --> 49:47.099
This is...

675
49:47.099 --> 49:49.318
What is it? What's wrong?

676
49:49.318 --> 49:51.951
Well? Is it that good?

677
49:53.083 --> 49:54.783
It's not like that.

678
49:56.636 --> 49:58.143
[Lost Time]

679
49:58.143 --> 50:00.036
[Written by Chu Si Hwan]

680
50:19.996 --> 50:21.420
What is it?

681
50:23.956 --> 50:25.656
We found him.

682
50:32.476 --> 50:34.114
You.

683
50:34.114 --> 50:36.232
Stop making me uncomfortable.

684
50:37.576 --> 50:40.336
What do you mean by that?

685
50:40.336 --> 50:42.600
Did I do something wrong?

686
50:42.600 --> 50:45.684
Saving me from danger.

687
50:45.684 --> 50:48.616
Making me feel guilty over you getting hurt because of me.

688
50:48.616 --> 50:51.834
Giving me help that I never even asked for, and making me feel sorry for it.

689
50:51.834 --> 50:53.913
I hate it.

690
50:56.863 --> 51:02.476
"The two men, Yeong Hyeon and Jae Yoon, don't hold back in their fight.

691
51:02.476 --> 51:04.156
Eun Soo cries out..."

692
51:04.156 --> 51:05.970
- Stop it! - "Stop. Stop it..."

693
51:05.970 --> 51:07.670
Please, stop.

694
51:10.596 --> 51:13.683
"The camcorder in Jae Yoon's hand

695
51:13.683 --> 51:16.720
falls to the ground...

696
51:16.720 --> 51:20.168
As the battery falls out of the camcorder,

697
51:20.168 --> 51:21.769
fade-out."

698
51:23.410 --> 51:25.110
What is this?

699
51:29.390 --> 51:30.830
[Ye Rang]

700
51:33.376 --> 51:34.887
Yes, Woo Jae?

701
51:34.887 --> 51:38.023
It's me. I read the script.

702
51:38.023 --> 51:39.776
The script? Which one?

703
51:39.776 --> 51:41.374
Anything catch your eye?

704
51:41.374 --> 51:43.921
"Lost Time." Director Chu Si Hwan.

705
51:44.584 --> 51:47.374
Do you know the director, by any chance?

706
51:47.374 --> 51:50.251
No, he's a rookie, so I've never even met him yet.

707
51:50.251 --> 51:51.775
What's the matter?

708
51:51.775 --> 51:55.316
Well... Have you read it yourself?

709
51:55.316 --> 52:01.073
Not yet. You do know that you get a truckload of scripts, right?

710
52:02.036 --> 52:04.100
This... Chu Si Hwan.

711
52:04.100 --> 52:05.491
Is that his real name?

712
52:05.491 --> 52:07.882
I don't know.

713
52:07.882 --> 52:11.090
We're meeting later today, so I'll check and get back to you.

714
52:11.090 --> 52:12.396
You're meeting today?

715
52:12.396 --> 52:13.416
Yeah,

716
52:13.416 --> 52:17.456
the development team was so pushy about getting Ha Na to meet this guy.

717
52:17.456 --> 52:20.967
The director did say that he wanted Ha Na as the female lead,

718
52:20.967 --> 52:24.418
and it's a really good script, so they wanted to seal the deal.

719
52:24.418 --> 52:28.747
Besides, Ha Na has no reason to decline a lead role at this point.

720
52:28.747 --> 52:30.818
When? Where?

721
52:32.087 --> 52:35.177
- Hey, Soo Hyuk. Let's go. - Yes, sir!

722
52:47.074 --> 52:48.447
[Destination: Haesol Pine Trail]

723
53:00.274 --> 53:03.279
The person who knows the secret of our camcorder,

724
53:03.279 --> 53:07.030
tried to hide it away...

725
53:07.030 --> 53:08.524
And...

726
53:09.594 --> 53:14.003
the one who deliberately dropped it in front of my own eyes.

727
53:15.180 --> 53:16.976
It's all him.

728
53:17.687 --> 53:19.320
Chu Si Hwan?

729
53:22.147 --> 53:23.174
[Ye Rang]

730
53:26.207 --> 53:27.504
Yeah, Ye Rang?

731
53:27.504 --> 53:30.575
Ha Na, don't freak out and listen carefully.

732
53:30.575 --> 53:33.532
Woo Jae is on his way to Haesol.

733
53:33.532 --> 53:36.398
He's going to be on "One and Only Table!"

734
53:36.398 --> 53:38.358
Really? That's great.

735
53:38.358 --> 53:40.482
I'll arrive there soon,

736
53:40.482 --> 53:42.106
but I just have one thing to say, as the trusted adult here.

737
53:42.106 --> 53:45.245
Just be careful, it must've been a hard decision for him.

738
53:45.245 --> 53:46.776
Don't you dare hug him.

739
53:46.776 --> 53:48.280
Don't even touch him!

740
53:48.280 --> 53:51.250
Yeah, babe, I mean, Ye Rang!

741
53:51.250 --> 53:54.098
Have you read the script for "Lost Time" yet?

742
53:54.098 --> 53:56.865
Not yet. I had so many other ones to go through.

743
53:56.865 --> 53:58.996
Why? Is it any good?

744
53:58.996 --> 54:01.266
Have you met the director?

745
54:01.266 --> 54:03.958
Is it someone you know?

746
54:03.958 --> 54:07.932
Everyone wants to know about Director Chu Si Hwan today, huh?

747
54:07.932 --> 54:11.102
- Huh? - Woo Jae just asked me about him, too.

748
54:11.102 --> 54:13.105
But I don't know him at all.

749
54:13.105 --> 54:15.154
Is the script that good?

750
55:00.505 --> 55:02.478
[One and Only Table]

751
55:03.505 --> 55:04.622
Chef.

752
55:04.622 --> 55:06.666
We have everything ready, just as you asked.

753
55:06.666 --> 55:09.065
But the main dish and cutlery that the prop team got

754
55:09.065 --> 55:11.836
are too reflective when filmed from the top-down.

755
55:11.836 --> 55:15.457
So, can I swap them out with the matte ones?

756
55:18.912 --> 55:21.542
Yeah, sure, let's do that.

757
55:21.542 --> 55:22.966
Yes, chef.

758
55:24.985 --> 55:26.742
You little imbecile!

759
55:26.742 --> 55:29.313
Who taught you so well, huh?

760
55:29.313 --> 55:31.415
Did you just slap my butt?

761
55:34.785 --> 55:36.271
Ha Na.

762
55:37.005 --> 55:38.765
What are you doing?

763
55:38.765 --> 55:41.371
I'm just proud of him.

764
55:57.334 --> 55:59.625
It's time, why isn't he here?

765
56:14.245 --> 56:15.916
- There you are. - Hello.

766
56:15.916 --> 56:17.452
- We'll do the interview first. - Okay.

767
56:17.452 --> 56:19.152
Come this way.

768
56:21.392 --> 56:23.523
- Right this way. - Oh, right.

769
56:36.376 --> 56:39.678
Woo Jae made a big decision today. I'm so proud of him.

770
56:39.678 --> 56:41.610
Thank you, Jung Woo Jae.

771
56:42.365 --> 56:44.782
Thank you so much, Woo Jae.

772
56:44.782 --> 56:46.733
It's for Ha Ru's sake.

773
56:46.733 --> 56:48.657
I'd do whatever I can to help him out.

774
56:48.657 --> 56:51.191
Wow, Woo Jae, you're so loyal!

775
56:54.038 --> 56:55.738
Hey, Seok Min!

776
56:58.085 --> 57:01.542
- Yes, ma'am. - Where is Director Chu Si Hwan now?

777
57:01.542 --> 57:03.005
One moment.

778
57:05.278 --> 57:09.409
Director Chu Si Hwan apparently came to Haesol on business, too.

779
57:09.409 --> 57:10.998
That's why I set the meeting up for today.

780
57:10.998 --> 57:12.438
You've all heard, right?

781
57:12.438 --> 57:14.349
If you come up a little further...

782
57:14.349 --> 57:16.393
You see me, right?

783
57:16.393 --> 57:18.091
This way!

784
57:18.091 --> 57:19.372
Hello.

785
57:19.372 --> 57:20.863
Let's go inside.

786
57:23.605 --> 57:25.761
Director Chu is here.

787
57:47.781 --> 57:50.011
Director Chu Si Hwan...

788
57:50.011 --> 57:52.137
was you, Jun Mo?

789
57:53.125 --> 57:55.225
It's been a while. Everyone.

790
57:57.005 --> 57:58.401
Woo Jae, you too.

791
58:01.925 --> 58:03.422
And Ha Na.

792
58:06.552 --> 58:08.992
I missed you guys. A lot.

793
58:50.491 --> 58:51.935
I...

794
58:51.935 --> 58:54.721
wish the characters in my movie were actually alive.

795
58:55.617 --> 58:56.897
The camcorder.

796
58:56.897 --> 58:58.897
How did you find it?

797
58:58.897 --> 59:00.622
We need to find out everything about that bastard.

798
59:00.622 --> 59:02.295
That way, we can at least try to stop him.

799
59:02.295 --> 59:04.465
The version of us...

800
59:04.465 --> 59:06.025
that we've lost.

801
59:06.644 --> 59:10.337
For the protagonist to have a strong motivation to travel back in time,

802
59:11.704 --> 59:14.161
someone would have to die.

803
59:14.161 --> 59:16.681
This is the only way to avert that fate.

804
59:17.311 --> 59:19.011
I need to stop.
